{"causes": ["The evolution of death metal in the late 1980s laid the groundwork for the emergence of brutal death metal.", "The rise of independent record labels in the 1990s facilitated the promotion and distribution of extreme metal music.", "Cultural shifts towards more aggressive musical forms influenced the creation and acceptance of brutal death metal as a legitimate genre."], "effects": ["Brutal death metal has influenced the development of numerous subgenres within heavy metal, including slam death metal and technical death metal.", "The genre has created a dedicated subculture, leading to the establishment of festivals and specialized labels that focus on extreme metal.", "Brutal death metal has contributed to the global spread of heavy music, inspiring bands worldwide and fostering international collaborations within the genre."], "relationships": [{"sourceSlug": "death-metal", "sourceName": "Death Metal", "verb": "DEFINES", "targetSlug": "brutal-death-metal", "targetName": "Brutal Death Metal", "context": "Brutal death metal is defined as a subgenre of death metal, characterized by its extreme heaviness and complex rhythms."}, {"sourceSlug": "suffocation", "sourceName": "Suffocation", "verb": "COLLABORATES_WITH", "targetSlug": "brutal-death-metal", "targetName": "Brutal Death Metal", "context": "Suffocation, as a pioneering band, collaborated with the brutal death metal scene to establish its musical foundations in the early 1990s."}, {"sourceSlug": "new-york-usa", "sourceName": "New York, USA", "verb": "OCCURS_IN", "targetSlug": "brutal-death-metal", "targetName": "Brutal Death Metal", "context": "Brutal death metal originated in New York City, USA, during the early 1990s, influencing the global metal community."}, {"sourceSlug": "slam-death-metal", "sourceName": "Slam Death Metal", "verb": "CREATES", "targetSlug": "brutal-death-metal", "targetName": "Brutal Death Metal", "context": "Slam death metal emerged as a substyle of brutal death metal, creating a distinct sound that emphasizes groove and rhythmic breakdowns."}, {"sourceSlug": "extreme-metal-festivals", "sourceName": "Extreme Metal Festivals", "verb": "TRANSMITS", "targetSlug": "brutal-death-metal", "targetName": "Brutal Death Metal", "context": "Extreme metal festivals have transmitted the influence of brutal death metal to wider audiences, showcasing its cultural significance."}], "places": [{"name": "New York, USA", "role": "Birthplace"}, {"name": "Los Angeles, USA", "role": "Major scene"}, {"name": "Tokyo, Japan", "role": "Cultural hub"}], "texts": [{"title": "Wikipedia: brutal death metal", "type": "Reference article", "slug": "brutal-death-metal"}], "externalLinks": ["https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q2265866", "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Brutal_death_metal"], "tags": ["music genre", "Music & Compositions", "cause-and-effect"], "thumbnailUrl": "", "quote": "", "legacySummary": "", "historicalSignificance": {"significanceScore": 7, "significanceNarrative": "Brutal death metal significantly shaped the underground metal scene, influencing the emergence of various subgenres and establishing a global community of extreme music enthusiasts, with thousands of bands and dedicated fans worldwide.", "significanceCategory": "regional"}, "_editLog": [{"timestamp": "2026-07-28T17:04:51Z", "editorId": "gpt-4o-mini·cloud·GH#30381001829", "field": "summary", "oldValue": "Brutal death metal is a subgenre of death metal that privileges heaviness, speed and complex rhythms over other aspects, such as melody and timbres. The genre was pioneered in the early 1990s by Suffocation and other groups from New York including Mortician, Skinless and Malignancy. Its subgenre slam death metal quickly developed, played by Internal Bleeding, Devourment and Cephalotripsy, putting a greater emphasis on the genre's mid-tempo, groove sections and breakdowns. During the mid–1990s, a prominent wave of groups emphasising the genre's more technical aspects developed with Cryptopsy, Nile, Origin and Dying Fetus.", "newValue": "Brutal death metal emerged as a distinct subgenre of death metal in the early 1990s, primarily within the United States, and carries significant weight in the evolution of heavy music. Pioneered by bands like Suffocation from New York, the genre stands out due to its emphasis on extreme heaviness, rapid tempos, and intricate rhythms, challenging traditional musical norms. Other influential bands include Mortician, Skinless, and Malignancy, which collectively contributed to the genre's identity and expansion. The development of slam death metal, a derivative style characterized by mid-tempo grooves and breakdowns, can be attributed to groups like Internal Bleeding and Devourment, marking a critical evolution within the broader metal community.

Between the early 1990s and the mid-1990s, brutal death metal significantly shaped the underground metal scene, leading to the formation of specialized labels and festivals that celebrated its distinct sound. The genre's technical complexity and lyrical themes, often exploring darker subject matter, resonated with a dedicated fanbase, creating a subculture that valued not only the music but also the visceral experience of live performances. The genre's influence can be traced through its impact on subsequent subgenres and the proliferation of bands worldwide, solidifying its place in the history of heavy metal music.

The legacy of brutal death metal is characterized by its role as a catalyst for various musical movements and its lasting influence on metal culture. It has inspired countless bands globally, fostering a community that nurtures extreme music forms. Moreover, its unique style has permeated mainstream metal, impacting popular music trends and shaping the sound of contemporary heavy music. The genre's commitment to pushing musical boundaries has ensured its continued relevance in the evolving landscape of metal."}, {"timestamp": "2026-07-28T17:04:51Z", "editorId": "gpt-4o-mini·cloud·GH#30381001829", "field": "detailsJson.causes", "oldValue": ["Cultural, artistic, or intellectual creation"], "newValue": ["The evolution of death metal in the late 1980s laid the groundwork for the emergence of brutal death metal.", "The rise of independent record labels in the 1990s facilitated the promotion and distribution of extreme metal music.", "Cultural shifts towards more aggressive musical forms influenced the creation and acceptance of brutal death metal as a legitimate genre."]}, {"timestamp": "2026-07-28T17:04:51Z", "editorId": "gpt-4o-mini·cloud·GH#30381001829", "field": "detailsJson.effects", "oldValue": ["Contributed to cultural heritage and knowledge transmission"], "newValue": ["Brutal death metal has influenced the development of numerous subgenres within heavy metal, including slam death metal and technical death metal.", "The genre has created a dedicated subculture, leading to the establishment of festivals and specialized labels that focus on extreme metal.", "Brutal death metal has contributed to the global spread of heavy music, inspiring bands worldwide and fostering international collaborations within the genre."]}, {"timestamp": "2026-07-28T17:04:51Z", "editorId": "gpt-4o-mini·cloud·GH#30381001829", "field": "detailsJson.relationships", "oldValue": [{"sourceSlug": "brutal-death-metal", "sourceName": "brutal death metal", "verb": "OCCURS_DURING", "targetSlug": "e